
=== absolute dry-mass scale, alpha = 0.185 mL/g ===
  prefactor lambda/(2 pi alpha)   0.572958 pg/(rad*um^2)
  literature range                0.173 - 0.215 mL/g
  systematic band on ANY absolute mass   +6.9% / -14.0%

  Relative metrics (dry_mass_mape, mass ratio, relative bias) are
  INVARIANT to alpha: the same constant multiplies the predicted and
  the reference mass and cancels. Do not sweep alpha hoping to move
  them, and do not attribute any part of the mass error to alpha.

  --- off_axis (1852 matched cells) ---
    mean reference dry mass     188.65 pg   [162.33, 201.73] pg from alpha alone
    mean predicted dry mass     173.46 pg
    dry-mass MAPE at alpha = 0.185    0.188688
    dry-mass MAPE at alpha = 0.215    0.188688   <- identical, as it must be

  --- gabor (1691 matched cells) ---
    mean reference dry mass     193.60 pg   [166.58, 207.03] pg from alpha alone
    mean predicted dry mass     186.41 pg
    dry-mass MAPE at alpha = 0.185    0.236591
    dry-mass MAPE at alpha = 0.215    0.236591   <- identical, as it must be

  -> runs/mass_uncertainty.json

  For the paper: quote absolute dry mass as  m +/- (systematic, alpha)
  using the band above, and quote MAPE without an alpha caveat, because
  it does not have one.
